Constitution: SDD

Purpose:
  Default engineering principles that apply to all projects.
  These are heuristics, not absolute laws. Exceptions require
  documented rationale.

Principles:
  SOLID:
    SRP: Single Responsibility
    OCP: Open/Closed
    LSP: Liskov Substitution
    ISP: Interface Segregation
    DIP: Dependency Inversion

  DRY:
    Avoid accidental duplication.
    Exception: duplication is acceptable when abstraction would couple unrelated domains.

  KISS:
    Prefer simpler solution.
    Exception: complexity is acceptable when it provides measurable business/technical value.

  YAGNI:
    Do not build until needed.
    Exception: building is acceptable when the cost of delay exceeds the cost of building.

  CleanCode:
    Readability, naming, structure, minimal comments.

  CleanArchitecture:
    Separation of concerns, dependency direction, explicit boundaries.

  FailFast:
    Detect and report errors immediately.

  LeastKnowledge:
    Modules should not know about internal details of other modules.

  CompositionOverInheritance:
    Prefer composition to inheritance.

  SeparationOfConcerns:
    Each module/component has exactly one reason to change.

Rules:
  [C1] Principles are default heuristics, not absolute laws.
  [C2] Exceptions to principles MUST be documented with rationale.
  [C3] Principle conflicts MUST be resolved by project-specific decisions.
  [C4] Constitution applies before architecture, which applies before skills, which apply before code.

